# Accepted-risk CVEs for this image, one per line:
#   CVE-ID exp:YYYY-MM-DD # reason
# `exp:` is a native Trivy feature - once the date passes, Trivy stops
# honoring the entry and the scan fails again, so these don't rot silently.
# Re-scan `postgres:18-trixie` before the expiry below; if upstream has
# rebuilt the tag with a patched Go toolchain/openssl, drop the
# corresponding lines instead of just pushing the date out.

# Bundled Go toolchain (go1.24.6) inside the postgres:18-trixie image
# itself, not anything we build - dozens of stdlib CVEs, all "fixed"
# upstream in a newer Go release that hasn't been rebuilt into this image
# tag yet.
